 "language": "en",
 "text": "306 people vanished on this ship in 1918, no distress call, no wreckage, everyone assumed a German U -boat got her, they were wrong. German naval records checked after the war, show zero submarines anywhere near her position, no one ever claimed the kill, because no one was there, so what actually happened? She was carrying ore five times denser than the coal she was built for, one of her two engines was broken, and she was so overloaded, her waterline mark was fully underwater when she left port, avern she sailed straight into a gale, case status, probable. She wasn't sunk by the war she was sailing through, she was killed by her own physics, full case file, the whole investigation, linked below.",
